arguments.prompt:
You need to build a Blazor Interactive Server recipe feature in the project at `/tmp/sv-b80d7a12468b4542a5fa1a062ddda5c6`.

The project is a .NET 11 Blazor Web App with Interactive Server (per-page) rendering. The root namespace is `sv_b80d7a12468b4542a5fa1a062ddda5c6`.

## Existing structure
- `Components/Pages/` has existing pages (Home.razor, Counter.razor, etc.)
- `Components/_Imports.razor` has standard Blazor usings
- `Program.cs` registers Razor components with `.AddInteractiveServerComponents()`
- The csproj has `BlazorDisableThrowNavigationException` set to true

## What to create

### 1. Models (`Models/Recipe.cs`)
Create a `Recipe` record with: `int Id`, `string Title`, `string Description`, `int PrepTimeMinutes`.

### 2. Service interface and implementation (`Services/IRecipeService.cs` and `Services/RecipeService.cs`)
- Interface: `IRecipeService` with method `Task<List<Recipe>> GetByCuisineAsync(int cuisineId, CancellationToken cancellationToken)`
- Implementation: `RecipeService`
  - Has hardcoded seed data for 3 cuisines (cuisine IDs 1, 2, 3 — e.g. Italian, Mexican, Japanese)
  - Each cuisine should have 4-5 recipes with realistic data
  - Simulates a slow API call with `await Task.Delay(2000, cancellationToken)` before returning
  - If cuisineId doesn't match any known cuisine, return an empty list
  - The cancellation token must be passed to Task.Delay so cancellation works

### 3. Register the service in `Program.cs`
Add `builder.Services.AddScoped<IRecipeService, RecipeService>();` and appropriate using statement.

### 4. Recipes page (`Components/Pages/Recipes.razor`)
This is the most complex part. Create an interactive Blazor Server page at route `/recipes/{CuisineId:int}`.

**Route and parameters:**
- `@page "/recipes/{CuisineId:int}"`
- `@rendermode InteractiveServer`
- `[Parameter] public int CuisineId { get; set; }`
- `[SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "sort")] public string? Sort { get; set; }` — accepts "newest" or "popular", defaults to "newest"
- Inject `IRecipeService`, `ILogger<Recipes>`, and `NavigationManager`

**Critical async lifecycle handling — implement with `SetParametersAsync`:**

Override `SetParametersAsync` (NOT `OnParametersSetAsync`) for full control. The pattern:

```csharp
public override async Task SetParametersAsync(ParameterView parameters)
{
    // Capture old CuisineId before base applies new values
    var previousCuisineId = CuisineId;

    await base.SetParametersAsync(parameters);

    // After base call, CuisineId and Sort have new values
    // Only reload if CuisineId actually changed (or first load)
    if (CuisineId != previousCuisineId)
    {
        await LoadRecipesAsync();
    }
}
```

**State management — use these fields:**
```
private List<Recipe>? _recipes;           // null = never loaded
private bool _isLoading;                   // true during any load
private bool _hasExistingData;             // true when _recipes was non-null before reload started  
private string? _errorMessage;             // non-null = error state
private bool _isTimeout;                   // true when error was specifically a timeout
private CancellationTokenSource? _loadCts; // for cancelling in-flight loads
```

**LoadRecipesAsync method:**
```csharp
private async Task LoadRecipesAsync()
{
    // Cancel any in-flight request
    await CancelPendingLoad();

    _loadCts = new CancellationTokenSource();
    var cancellationToken = _loadCts.Token;

    _hasExistingData = _recipes is { Count: > 0 };
    _isLoading = true;
    _errorMessage = null;
    _isTimeout = false;
    StateHasChanged();

    try
    {
        var results = await RecipeService.GetByCuisineAsync(CuisineId, cancellationToken);

        // Don't update if cancelled while awaiting
        if (cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested) return;

        _recipes = results;
        _isLoading = false;
        StateHasChanged();
    }
    catch (OperationCanceledException) when (cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested)
    {
        // Intentional cancellation — do nothing, a new load is taking over
    }
    catch (TimeoutException ex)
    {
        Logger.LogError(ex, "Timeout loading recipes for cuisine {CuisineId}", CuisineId);
        _isLoading = false;
        _isTimeout = true;
        _errorMessage = "The request timed out. Please try again.";
        StateHasChanged();
    }
    catch (Exception ex) when (ex is not OperationCanceledException)
    {
        Logger.LogError(ex, "Error loading recipes for cuisine {CuisineId}", CuisineId);
        _isLoading = false;
        _errorMessage = "Something went wrong while loading recipes. Please try again.";
        StateHasChanged();
    }
}
```

**CancelPendingLoad helper:**
```csharp
private async ValueTask CancelPendingLoad()
{
    if (_loadCts is not null)
    {
        await _loadCts.CancelAsync();
        _loadCts.Dispose();
        _loadCts = null;
    }
}
```

**Retry method:**
```csharp
private async Task RetryAsync()
{
    await LoadRecipesAsync();
}
```

**Implement `IAsyncDisposable`:**
```csharp
public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
{
    await CancelPendingLoad();
}
```

**UI Rendering (the markup section):**

```razor
@page "/recipes/{CuisineId:int}"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@implements IAsyncDisposable
@inject IRecipeService RecipeService
@inject ILogger<Recipes> Logger
@inject NavigationManager Navigation

<PageTitle>Recipes</PageTitle>

<h1>Recipes</h1>

@if (_errorMessage is not null)
{
    <div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert">
        <p>@_errorMessage</p>
        <button class="btn btn-outline-danger" @onclick="RetryAsync">Retry</button>
    </div>
}
else if (_isLoading && !_hasExistingData)
{
    <p><em>Loading recipes...</em></p>
}
else if (_recipes is not null)
{
    @if (_isLoading && _hasExistingData)
    {
        <div class="alert alert-info" role="status">
            <em>Refreshing…</em>
        </div>
    }

    var sorted = GetSortedRecipes();

    @if (sorted.Count == 0)
    {
        <p>No recipes found for this cuisine.</p>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="row">
            @foreach (var recipe in sorted)
            {
                <div class="col-md-4 mb-3">
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5 class="card-title">@recipe.Title</h5>
                            <p class="card-text">@recipe.Description</p>
                            <span class="badge bg-secondary">@recipe.PrepTimeMinutes min</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    }
}
```

**GetSortedRecipes method** (sort is purely client-side, no reload):
```csharp
private List<Recipe> GetSortedRecipes()
{
    if (_recipes is null) return new();

    return Sort?.ToLowerInvariant() switch
    {
        "popular" => _recipes.OrderBy(r => r.PrepTimeMinutes).ToList(),
        _ => _recipes.OrderByDescending(r => r.Id).ToList() // "newest" is default
    };
}
```

### 5. Build verification
After creating all files, run `dotnet build` from the project directory to verify everything compiles.

